{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/3189","id":3526233229,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz887SLgyN","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3189","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3189.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3189.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3189","number":3189,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"types, util: normalise hostnames from hostinfo instead of rejecting","user":{"login":"ykhrustalev","id":737733,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNzczMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/737733?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ykhrustalev","html_url":"https://github.com/ykhrustalev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ykhrustalev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ykhrustalev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ykhrustalev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ykhrustalev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ykhrustalev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ykhrustalev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ykhrustalev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ykhrustalev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ykhrustalev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #3188.\r\n\r\nHostnames like `Joe's Mac mini` were dropped on registration (falling back to `invalid-<random>`) and then rejected on every MapRequest with `WRN Rejecting invalid hostname update from hostinfo`. Both paths now route through `util.NormaliseHostname`, which lowercases, strips characters outside `[a-z0-9-.]`, and truncates to 63 chars. The update is dropped only if the normalised value is still invalid (empty, or starts/ends with a dash). Existing `invalid-*` nodes self-heal on the next MapRequest.\r\n\r\n### Also changes\r\n\r\nOther previously-rejected inputs now succeed (all strictly more permissive, none silently corrupting):\r\n\r\n| Input | After |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `> 63 chars` | truncated to 63 |\r\n| `test_node` | `testnode` |\r\n| `Test@Host` | `testhost` |\r\n| `server-北京-01` | `server--01` |\r\n\r\nStill rejected: empty-after-strip (`🎉`, `@@@`), leading/trailing dash (`-test`, `test-`), too short.\r\n\r\n### Left for follow-up\r\n\r\n- `node.Hostname` is normalised but `node.Hostinfo.Hostname` keeps the raw client string. Peers get the normalised value via `tailcfg.Node.Name` and the raw via `Hostinfo` — matches Tailscale's model.\r\n- `GivenName` has a DB unique index. Two nodes across different users normalising to the same label will race; the losing MapRequest fails with a constraint error and the client retries. Rare and self-limiting. Wiring `EnsureUniqueGivenName` into the update path would fix it, at the cost of added complexity — happy to do it if wanted.\r\n\r\n<!-- Please tick if the following things apply. You… -->\r\n\r\n- [x] have read the [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md) file\r\n- [x] raised a GitHub issue or discussed it on the projects chat beforehand\r\n- [x] added unit tests\r\n- [ ] added integration tests\r\n- [ ] updated documentation if needed\r\n- [x] updated CHANGELOG.md\r\n","created_at":"2026-04-14T02:57:41Z","updated_at":"2026-04-19T01:39:56Z","closed_at":"2026-04-18T14:12:24Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"a2c1edfd14b9615157dc5b96c04fd4ded5023372","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krad